There are a few points to consider:

- It works reasonably well, though evaluation is needed to measure performance.

- It cannot work all the time due to many assumptions; later chapters will improve this approach for general images.

Despite limitations, many general ideas carry over to more sophisticated solutions (e.g., gathering and propagating local evidence). One question is how 3D orientation information given at edges propagates to flat image areas to produce correct solutions there.

